      "content": "I am currently investigating intermittent latency spikes and jitter on a specific subnet in our Lyon POP. We are seeing significant variance in RTT which is impacting VoIP traffic quality. \n\nPlease analyze the following hop data and let me know if the pattern suggests a physical layer degradation (e.g., failing SFP or fiber issues) or if this looks like a typical queuing delay/congestion issue.\n\nHop 4 (85.22.14.2):\n- RTT Min: 54.2ms\n- RTT Max: 215.8ms\n- RTT Avg: 88.4ms\n- Packet Loss: 4%\n\nHop 5 (85.22.15.1):\n- RTT Min: 142.1ms\n- RTT Max: 192.5ms\n- RTT Avg: 155.3ms\n- Packet Loss: 12%\n\nThe jitter on Hop 4 is particularly erratic. What is your assessment?",
